{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789334820,"nonce":"0bUAeCheiuApbqHX5nt4Qv2pp50=","title":"Cranelift bodies record stack maps the Immix collector never reads","message":"Every Wren value at a block parameter was stored to its own stack slot\non block entry and reloaded after calls, because the frontend's user\nstack maps spill marked values; collect_garbage only reads the\nresulting metadata for the non-Immix collectors, and Immix scans the\nnative stack conservatively. The default collector is Immix, so this\nwas a store per live value per loop iteration for nothing (the tally\nsetter loop: four stores at the header).\n\nNow stack maps are marked only when a collector that needs precise\nroots exists in the process (the same counter that gates write\nbarriers) or for AOT, whose collector is unknown at compile time.\nFrame pointers stay preserved either way; the conservative scanner\nwalks them. Mac, baseline tier: setter 3.60 -\u003e 3.51, construct 5.35 -\u003e\n4.99; delta_blue 0.0588 -\u003e 0.0508 s, binary_trees 0.143 -\u003e 0.129,\nmethod_call 0.0200 -\u003e 0.0186 (WLIFT_DISABLE_STACK_MAPS=1 A/B).","files":null}]}